    "name": "propose",
    "description": "Propose sending a prompt to Codex (OpenAI's coding agent, on the user's ChatGPT subscription) for an independent, read-only second opinion. The user sees your reason and the full prompt in the Cockpit pane, picks the model and approves or declines. Returns at once: do not wait or poll. If approved, Codex runs read-only in the project folder and its answer reaches you later as a new message; if declined, you are told. Codex does not see this conversation: make the prompt self-contained (goal, absolute paths of the plan or files to read, what to check, what form the answer should take). Write `why` in Hebrew for the user; the prompt in English."
   }
